# Review: OsrmPlugin

The routing half of the milestone is built and tested. plugin-osrm contributes `makeOsrmRoutingService`
(Nominatim geocoding plus OSRM routing) under `TripCapabilities.RoutingService`, with fixture tests for
the mapping and a mocked-fetch test for the service. plugin-trip has the `Routing` DTOs, the
`RoadDetails.routes` field, the `PlanRoute` operation (tested), a "Plan route" toolbar action, and a
marker provider that draws the routed polyline.

The plugin-map half is not built. There is no `TileProvider` registry, no `tileProvider` setting and no
bespoke settings surface; `buildTileUrl` still hardcodes MapTiler `streets-v2` from a `maptiler.com` key.

Of 9 items: 2 done, 3 untested, 0 partial, 1 diverged, 3 missing.

